  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Let $c=\u27e82,-1,6\u27e9$ and $d=\u27e84,-2,10\u27e9.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=\u27e8$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 10}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}}d \\\\  & =\\frac{70}{120}\u27e84,-2,10\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}\u27e84,-2,10\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\,\\frac{7}{3},-\\frac{7}{6},\\frac{35}{6}\\,\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
